# /apps/afterframe/ (trailing slash) was the app's canonical, live URL before
# it was renamed to Aftershot — see astro.config.mjs's `redirects` entry for
# the non-slash form. /apps/* is excluded from the Worker (dist/_routes.json),
# so Cloudflare's static-asset layer matches these rules as literal strings
# with no trailing-slash normalization; the config-generated rule alone would
# 404 on this exact form. Kept as a raw rule here because Astro's `redirects`
# config collapses a trailing-slash key onto the same route as the non-slash
# one, so it cannot express this as a second config entry.
/apps/afterframe/    /apps/aftershot/    301
